// t128 division and remainder. The interpreter computes them; Cranelift's x64
// backend has no 128-bit divide — `%` PANICKED inside the code generator (exit
// 2) and `/` failed to compile — so the JIT now refuses them cleanly (SKIP).
a: t128 = 7
b: t128 = 2
q: t128 = a / b
r: t128 = a % b
y: t64 = q
z: t64 = r
print(y)
print(z)
